<%#
  Stand-in for the solana-studio gem's contributed credential button.

  studio-engine does not depend on solana-studio, and must not: the base
  template cannot depend on the bolt-on that extends it. So the seam is proven
  against a fixture on an extra view path, which is exactly the shape the gem's
  app/views takes in a real host. What is asserted is that the ENGINE finds and
  renders whatever sits at this path, not what the gem happens to draw there.
%>
<button type="button"
        x-show="methodOn('wallet')"
        data-contributed-credential="wallet"
        @click="attested() && $store.<%= local_assigns.fetch(:modal_store) %>.swap('wallet-connect', { backTo: 'auth', ageAttested: true })">
  CONTRIBUTED-WALLET-CTA
</button>
